WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.750
Before anything goes into an AI tool, tier it.

2
00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.199
There are four tiers, and the highest one

3
00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:09.312
in your input decides where it can go.

4
00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:13.496
Public is approved for public release, like the

5
00:00:13.554 --> 00:00:14.494
course catalog.

6
00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:17.408
Internal is routine business with low harm if

7
00:00:17.478 --> 00:00:19.707
exposed, like budget meeting notes.

8
00:00:20.218 --> 00:00:24.096
Confidential means exposure would harm people or operations,

9
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.826
like a firewall log.

10
00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:30.620
Restricted is protected by law, regulation, or contract.

11
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.627
For Restricted, name the law.

12
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.867
A class roster with IDs and grades is

13
00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.539
an education record, so FERPA.

14
00:00:37.864 --> 00:00:39.931
A financial aid appeal is FERPA plus the

15
00:00:40.001 --> 00:00:41.672
GLBA Safeguards Rule.

16
00:00:42.972 --> 00:00:43.843
Now the rule.

17
00:00:44.168 --> 00:00:46.966
Paste meeting notes with the roster underneath, and

18
00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:49.114
the highest tier is Restricted, so the whole

19
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.321
input is Restricted.

20
00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:52.457
Consumer chatbot: no.

21
00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:55.453
Licensed enterprise tool: not by default.

22
00:00:55.894 --> 00:01:00.015
Managed campus server: only de-identified, logged, with set retention.

23
00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.384
Unmanaged laptop: no.

24
00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:04.604
Pause here.

25
00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:06.670
Tier the reported phishing email.

26
00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:08.772
Then name the highest tier in a paste

27
00:01:08.795 --> 00:01:11.105
that mixes the catalog entry with a financial

28
00:01:11.163 --> 00:01:12.011
aid appeal.
